HEALTHCARE ECONOMICS REDESIGN: REGIONAL ADVOCATE MODEL
Handoff Document | Comprehensive yet Terse

================================================================================
CORE MECHANISM
================================================================================

REGIONAL UNITS: 20,000-person regions. Advocates (business-model agnostic: 
actuaries, clinics, gyms, etc.) bid via reverse Vickrey auction.

AUCTION LOGIC:
  - Bid = fixed price + bonus (expressed as expectation value)
  - Winner: lowest bid (fixed price + bonus expectation)
  - Winner's payment: second-lowest bid's total price
  - Winner's bonus: expands to match second-lowest bid's expectation value
  - Rationale: Incentivizes honest bidding; prevents winner's curse

TENURE & CONTINUITY:
  - Year 1: Fixed rate; single bonus paid after 12 months
  - Year 2+: Inflation-adjusted continuation (no re-bid) if healthy region
  - Unhealthy regions: Re-bid annually
  - Care transfer: Incoming Advocate auto-assumes all patients (no opt-out)
    Incentive: Advocate profits by retaining/improving inherited population

SANCTIONS:
  - Bottom 1/5th (annual ranking): Cannot bid on new regions
  - Lost >50% of regions: Cannot bid on new regions
  - Lost a region: Barred from immediate next auction; may bid in re-auction
    if no other bids received

================================================================================
ENTITIES & RESPONSIBILITIES
================================================================================

GOVERNMENT
  - Collects taxes; pays fixed rates + bonuses
  - Provides initial population metrics
  - Submits research bids; employs expert staff
  - Sets/updates bonus metrics (via governance process TBD)

AUCTION HOUSES (independent; profit or non-profit)
  - Anonymized data warehouses; manage secret bids
  - Package/resell research to Advocates, Government, manufacturers
  - Assign researchers to projects; validate researcher output
  - Operate as profit centers

ADVOCATES
  - Bid on regions; win at auction
  - Deliver or coordinate care; manage operations
  - Earn bonuses based on population health metrics
  - May collect copays (rules TBD)
  - Cannot participate in secondary markets (no mid-year transfers)

RESEARCHERS
  - Blinded to client identity; bid competitively on projects
  - Assigned by Auction Houses (top 2 bids; mismatch → 3rd/4th study)
  - Validated via billing codes, interviews, registries
  - Output: Metrics reporting, cost estimates, policy analysis

PATIENTS
  - Automatic transfer to new Advocate on region changeover
  - Retain freedom to seek external care at own expense
  - Open sandboxed connections to centralized records (via Auction Houses)

