BONUS METRICS (No Lagging; Inherently Slow-Moving)
================================================================================

PRIMARY METRICS:
  - Disability-Free Life Expectancy
  - Average Age of First Chronic Disease Diagnosis
  - Employment Rate (age 55–70)
  - Cost per Healthy Life Year Gained
  - Time to First Hospitalization
  - Mortality Rate (age-adjusted)
  - Hospital Readmission Rate (30-day)
  - Functional Independence
  - Healthcare Utilization Efficiency
  - Patient-Reported Health Status

HIGH-IMPACT DISPARITY METRICS (race-neutral statute; demographic tracking):
  - Maternal mortality/morbidity
  - Female AMI outcomes
  - Diabetes control
  - Opioid overdose/treatment
  - Colorectal cancer screening/mortality
  - Hypertension control
  - Breast cancer screening/mortality
  - Kidney disease progression
  - Mental health/suicide prevention
  - Prostate cancer screening/mortality

DATA SOURCES:
  - Insurance/pharmacy claims
  - Registries
  - Employment records
  - Hospital/ED data
  - Functional assessments
  - Surveys
  - Certificates

VALIDATION:
  - Constant inflation-adjusted budget
  - Draconian penalties for purposeful mis-reporting

BONUS FUNCTION DESIGN (TBD):
  - Sensitivity analysis via 3D color plot (health × cost × equity)
  - Avoid explicit function weights (β values) in white paper
  - Incentive structure must temper economic transition and set expected costs

DEMAND CURVE LOGIC:
  - Advocate incentives shift demand leftward (prevention, healthspan focus)
  - Expected shifts: 40–60% (low-value), 10–20% (moderate-value), 0–5% (high-value)
  - Cost = intersection of new demand curve + current supply curve
  - Benchmarks: Managed care (10–25% utilization ↓); Kaiser (15–25% leftward shift)
  - Cost-effectiveness thresholds: UK £20–30K/QALY; Australia A$50K/QALY; 
    US (implicit) $100–150K/QALY

